{"name":"Bit of Heaven","hex":"#cad7de","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Berinomo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small amount of something.","A piece of metal placed in a horse's mouth and connected to the reins to direct the animal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bit"},{"term":"heaven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sky, specifically:\n The distant sky in which the sun, moon, and stars appear or move; the firmament; the celestial spheres.\n\n The near sky in which weather, flying animals, etc. appear;  the atmosphere; the climate.\n\n A model displaying the movement of the celestial bodies, an orrery.","The distant sky in which the sun, moon, and stars appear or move; the firmament; the celestial spheres."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To transport to the abode of God, the gods, or the blessed.","To beatify, enchant, or please greatly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heaven"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bit","blocks":[{"text":"The bit is the most basic unit of information in computing and digital communication. The name is a portmanteau of binary digit. Its symbol is either \"bit\" or lowercase \"b\". Use of the latter may create confusion with capital \"B\", which is the international standard symbol for the byte."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bit","wikidata":"Q8805"},{"title":"Heaven","blocks":[{"text":"Heaven, or the Heavens, is a common religious cosmological or supernatural place where beings such as deities, angels, souls, saints, or venerated ancestors are said to originate, be enthroned, or reside. According to the beliefs of some religions, heavenly beings can descend to Earth or incarnate and earthly beings can ascend to Heaven in the afterlife or, in exceptional cases, enter Heaven without dying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Paradiso_Canto_3